WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:02.009
MARK MIRCHANDANI: A
surprise party might be fun,

00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:04.665
but a surprise on your
Cloud bill usually isn't.

00:00:04.665 --> 00:00:06.540
Thankfully, you can set
up budgets and alerts

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.630
using Google Cloud Platform
to closely monitor your costs

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.130
and work with the
appropriate teams

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.140
so that they can take
action if needed.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.920
On this episode of
"Beyond Your Bill,"

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.520
we'll talk about setting up
budgets and how you can get

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.560
notified when anything
unexpected happens.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.432
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.920
Setting a budget in GCP lets
you trigger notifications

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.110
when your costs hit
or are forecasted

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.270
to hit a specified amount.

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.760
You can set up a budget for
an entire billing account

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.040
or multiple budgets for
different combinations

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.560
of projects and GCP
products so that you

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.235
can stay informed on the
areas that matter most to you.

00:00:44.235 --> 00:00:45.610
Let's look at the
interface where

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:47.320
you can manage your
budgets, set one

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:50.563
up, and see what the options
for notifications are.

00:00:50.563 --> 00:00:52.480
We'll start by going to
the Budgets and Alerts

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.250
page in the GCP console.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.870
You can use the
top left navigation

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.630
to choose Billing, and then
select the billing account.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:01.150
From there, click on
Budgets and Alerts.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.650
Only billing account
administrators

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:04.930
are able to create or
update budgets and alerts

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:05.870
for a billing account.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.870
So make sure that you
have the right permissions

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.240
for the billing account
that you've chosen.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.250
On this page, you can
see all the budgets that

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.660
belong to this billing account.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.303
Each budget is made up of a
few different important pieces.

00:01:16.303 --> 00:01:18.220
First, you have the name
for the budget, which

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:19.678
is helpful for you
to identify what

00:01:19.678 --> 00:01:21.340
this budget is meant to track.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.760
Next is the budget type, which
can either be specified amount,

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.610
where you set a fixed amount to
compare your monthly spend to,

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.430
or last month's spend, where
you target an amount based

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:31.990
on the previous month's spend.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.365
We'll come back
to those when you

00:01:33.365 --> 00:01:34.840
walk through creating a budget.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.650
After that is the
scope of the budget,

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.640
which is the combinations
of projects and GCP products

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:40.840
that this budget covers.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.820
So you may have a budget for
your entire billing account,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.770
one for just your
production projects,

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.470
one for just your
BigQuery spend,

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.462
or multiple for any
combination of those.

00:01:49.462 --> 00:01:50.920
On the other side
of the budget are

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.830
the actual threshold details for
when the budget should send out

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.390
an alert notification.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:57.220
Each budget can have
multiple thresholds.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.470
And you can see an overview
of the current status

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.455
for each budget on this page.

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:03.580
The thresholds are percentages
of either the amount

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.980
you entered or the last
month's spend based

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.390
on the type of budget.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.580
You can always come to this
page to see your budgets

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.870
and click on one to edit it.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.402
Let's go through and create a
budget to see all the options.

00:02:13.402 --> 00:02:15.610
We'll do that by clicking
on the Create Budget button

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:16.427
at the top.

00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:18.260
The first screen is the
scope of the budget,

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:21.340
which includes the name,
projects, and products covered.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.080
If you don't choose any projects
or products from the dropdown,

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.860
this budget will default to
the entire billing account.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:28.960
Since you can set up as
many budgets as you want,

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.460
feel free to create
multiple budgets

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.980
to track different groups
of projects and products

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.780
based on your needs.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.630
On the next screen, you can
choose the type of budget.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.610
If you choose
specified amount, you

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:42.400
can choose a target amount for
this budget to track towards.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.858
Depending on the
cost you're trying

00:02:43.858 --> 00:02:47.800
to measure, that could be
$100, $100,000, or more.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.660
If you choose last
month's spend,

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.540
the amount will be pre-populated
with the spend from last month

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.730
based on the scope you
just chose and it'll

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.410
be updated every month.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:57.970
For example, if you
choose a product

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:00.040
that you haven't used
before or you've only

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:03.280
used within the free tier, this
amount may show up as zero.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.870
This can be a good
way to get notified

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.870
as soon as you start to
spend money on something

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.270
you didn't expect
to spend it on.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.187
In addition, you can
choose to include credits

00:03:10.187 --> 00:03:11.350
in the budget amount.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.780
Including credits means
you'll take the total cost

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.820
and then subtract any
credits that were applied

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.320
for that billing period.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:20.200
Credits may include things like
usage discounts, promotions,

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.130
or grants.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.692
On the next step, you'll be
able to set up the actions.

00:03:23.692 --> 00:03:25.150
You can set up
different thresholds

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.310
based on the amount from
the previous step for when

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.457
the alert notification
should trigger.

00:03:29.457 --> 00:03:31.540
For example, you may want
to set an alert for when

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.320
you've reached 50%, 90%,
and 100% of your budget

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:36.463
for the month.

00:03:36.463 --> 00:03:38.380
You can also add additional
thresholds in case

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.610
you want more granularity.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:44.020
And each threshold can be based
on actual or forecasted costs.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.690
Actual cost thresholds
trigger when

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:47.440
the spend from the
scope that you selected

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.490
exceeds the specified amount.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:52.750
For example, you could set up
a 50% actual cost threshold

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.780
on $1,000 budget, and you'll
get an alert notification

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:58.450
when your cost exceeds $500.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:00.310
Forecasted cost
thresholds trigger

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:02.830
when your cost is predicted
to exceed the threshold

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.720
amount by the end of the month.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.430
If you add a forecasted
cost threshold

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.790
for 110% on a $1,000
budget, it will

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.560
trigger an alert
notification as soon

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.630
as your cost for the
total billing period

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.750
is expected to hit
$1,100 even if you're

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.700
only a few days into the month.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.820
There is also an option for
connecting budget to pub/sub

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.220
for programmatic budget
notifications, which

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:27.070
let you add more advanced
cost controls to your budgets.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.870
We'll talk about that
in a later video.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.700
But you can check out the link
below for more information.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.420
Keep in mind that different
GCP products or services update

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.160
costs at different times.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.530
Most services will update
costs within an hour.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:41.260
But some may take up to
a full day to update.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.128
Each service has costs based
on different metrics as well.

00:04:44.128 --> 00:04:45.670
We recommend setting
multiple budgets

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.950
so that you can get
alerted as soon as possible

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:49.675
and take action.

00:04:49.675 --> 00:04:51.550
Once you save your
budget, you're good to go.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:54.190
Though, it may take a few
hours before it kicks in.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.870
Here's an email alert
that was sent out

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:59.350
for a budget that was set
to 100% for a $10 budget.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:02.040
We can see the display name of
the budget, the budget amount

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.830
and period, the triggering
threshold, and the associated

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.895
billing account ID in the email.

00:05:07.895 --> 00:05:10.270
It's also easy to get straight
to the Budget page in case

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:13.570
you want to see more information
or edit your budgets.

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.130
Only billing account
administrators

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.740
and billing account users
will get an email notification

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.940
for a budget alert.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:22.030
Remember, budget alerts are sent
out based on the rules you set,

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:24.550
but they don't actually stop
any usage from happening.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.150
If you want to go beyond
emails and automate actions,

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.880
you should consider using
quotas or programmatic budget

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.020
notifications.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.020
Both of which we'll talk
about in future videos.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.520
Check out the links below for
more information about setting

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.660
up budgets and alerts.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:40.610
[MUSIC PLAYING]

